xnu 0429: keep only the AP-owned SMPS votes in the WiFi sequence

Measured 2026-11-25 and 2026-11-26, including a cold power cycle: the worker
completes the five PM8350/PM8350C SMPS votes, then hangs on whichever shared
RSC resource it reaches first. The failing vote moved between mx.lvl, cx.lvl,
xo.lvl and SN7 across builds; skipping one only moved the hang to the next.

Keep the AP-owned SMPS (the WiFi rails) and skip the four shared ARC/XO/NoC
votes. They are performance levels, not power rails, and the bootloader's
values are what the link trained with. If W1 reports a link failure, the next
step is an AOP-owned vote, not another direct TCS write.

