-	 * xo.lvl is the RPMh XO clock resource. Measured 2026-11-25 and again
-	 * after a cold power cycle on 2026-11-26: the worker logs cx.lvl and then
-	 * the next vote never returns, so the RSC access is owned by the AOP and
-	 * the bootloader's XO configuration is what the link uses. Skip the vote
-	 * until the AOP path exists.
+	 * mx.lvl, cx.lvl, xo.lvl and SN7 are not AP-owned. Measured 2026-11-25
+	 * and 2026-11-26 across warm and cold boots: the worker completes the five
+	 * PM8350/PM8350C SMPS votes, then hangs on whichever of these four it
+	 * reaches first (mx, cx, xo or SN7 in different builds). The direct RSC
+	 * access wedges; the loader's levels are what the link trained with. Keep
+	 * the AP-owned SMPS and skip the shared votes until the AOP path exists.
 	 */
-	wifi_log("xo.lvl vote skipped; loader XO configuration retained");
+	wifi_log("ARC/XO/NoC votes skipped; loader levels retained");
 	/*
 	 * SN7 is the PCIe NoC bandwidth vote. Measured 2026-11-25: the direct RSC
